title: Askew's government lives on?
subtitle: Chancellor [+ chancellor +] has assembled a majority government.
new-page: true
view-if: marcher_in_government == 0 and marcher_toleration == 0 and chancellor = "Askew" and bourgeois_coalition >= 50 and not in_bourgeois_coalition and (not kvp_formed or young_plan_ratified)
on-arrival: bruning_event_seen = 1; marcher_in_government = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; in_bourgeois_coalition = 1; chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; foreign_minister_party = "Gold"; interior_minister_party = "Unionist"; justice_minister_party = "Unionist"; labor_minister_party = "Unionist"; reichswehr_minister_party = ddp_name; economic_minister_party = "Unionist"; finance_minister_party = "Unionist"; agriculture_minister_party = "Unionist"; bruning_event_timer = 0; bourgeois_cooperation += 10; unionist_relation -= 5; judicial_reform -= 1
tags: event
priority: -1
max-visits: 1

= actually what the hell

Following the collapse of the Grand coalition, President [+ president +] has appointed Heinrich Askew of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] in a government supported solely by bourgeois forces. Usually, these governments can't survive without toleration from the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> or the inclusion of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>. 

Somehow, a bourgeois coalition actually holds a majority in the Assembly, consisting of the plethora of parties between the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>. 

